.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-openpgp-access 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-openpgp\-access \- Manage PIN, Reset Code and Admin PIN
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-openpgp\-access\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage PIN, Reset Code and Admin PIN
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-set\-retries(1)
Set retry counters for PIN, Reset Code and Admin PIN
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-change\-pin(1)
Change the User PIN
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-change\-admin\-pin(1)
Change the Admin PIN
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-change\-reset\-code(1)
Set (or, with \-\-clear, remove) the Reset Code
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-unblock\-pin(1)
Unblock and set a new PIN using the Reset Code or the Admin PIN
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-set\-signature\-policy(1)
Set the signature PIN policy
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-set\-touch\-cache(1)
Set the card\-wide touch cache duration in seconds (0 disables caching)
.TP
ckman\-openpgp\-access\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
